<title>JAPAN: Toyota Jan domestic output up 30.9% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Toyota Jan domestic output up 30.9% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toyota Motor Corp said on Thursday that its domestic vehicle production rose 30.9 percent in January from a year earlier to 313,955 vehicles.</p>
<p>Toyota's exports rose 71.1 percent in January from a year earlier to 132,191 vehicles.  </p>
<p>Toyota's January domestic production rose for a seventh successive month on a year-on-year basis, reflecting higher domestic sales and exports.</p>
<p>Its vehicle exports rose for the first time in two months due to higher exports to the North America, Europe, and the Middle East.</p>
<p>Toyota's domestic sales rose for a fifth month in a row, reflecting strong demand for new recreational vehicles.</p>
<p>Toyota's domestic vehicle production, exports, domestic sales and overseas output in January were as follows:</p>
<p> Production	   313,955   up 30.9 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		262,862   up 34.9 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses   51,093   up 13.6 percent</p>
<p> Domestic sales     126,540   up 15.7 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		 80,865   up 12.9 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses   45,675   up 21.0 percent</p>
<p> Exports		132,191   up 71.1 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		102,136   up 71.2 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses   30,055   up 70.8 percent</p>
<p> Overseas output    118,580   up  9.5 percent</p>
</text>
